Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course!  Here's a simple example of an if/then statement in C:

```
int x = 5;

if (x > 0) {
    printf("x is positive\n");
} else if (x == 0) {
    printf("x is zero\n");
} else {
    printf("x is negative\n");
}
```

In this code, we use an if/then statement to check if the variable x is greater than zero, zero, or negative.  If it is positive, we print a message saying so.  If it is zero, we print a different message.  If it is negative, we print yet another different message.
